'''Balrog''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Street Fighter Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 10.0 Update|Version 10.0]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 572
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Balrog
|name2 = Balrog CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Balrog CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Balrog is one of the very few [[:Category:Focused Target Cats|Focused Target Cats]], a class of cat that attacks only a certain trait of enemy, but has enormous stats in return. Balrog's damage and health, while not even comparable to the likes of [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock & Pierre]] or [[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Takeda Shingen]], are nonetheless amazing enough that he effectively destroys his typing while remaining at a decently safe distance. With that being said, don't expect to use Balrog on stages where he won't attack.

The only class of enemy which Balrog targets, but may falter against is [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]]; as some can burrow into his standing range and chip off some of his HP. But that will happen rarely, as Balrog's decent knockback count and quick attack rate can make short work of those that do. Even against the toughest of enemies, like [[Dread Bore]], [[Razorback]], or [[J.K. Bun Bun|J.K. Bun Bun]], he will be able to stand his ground with protection. Additionally, Balrog has the [[Zombie Killer]] ability, which is an absolute must-have for [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|Anti-Zombie Cats]].

This unit has a usefully low cost, but also a long cooldown, making it so he can be sent out early into the battle, which is especially good for Zombie stages, as they are often cash-limited, but he can rarely be stacked or replaced in fights.

