==Trivia==
*In Japan, and by extension [[Nyanko Daisensou|Nyanko Daisensou]], this Fighter is instead known as [[M. Bison (Uber Rare Cat)|M. Bison]], while Balrog's name was originally assigned to [[Vega (Uber Rare Cat)|Vega]].
** This was likely done proactively when localizing Street Fighter II to avoid legal trouble from real life boxer Mike Tyson's legal team, as Balrog is based on him.
*** The title "Boxer" (Balrog), "Claw" ([[Vega (Uber Rare Cat)|Vega]]) and "Dictator" ([[M. Bison (Uber Rare Cat)|M. Bison]]) have been adopted to not cause confusion when referring to these three Shadaloo leaders between Japanese and international players.

